## REF1-R7-WORD-05 — README:83 no longer mis-routes 'implemented'

The sentence routed "accepted", "implemented" or a commit identity to the ledger,
while the sentence two above gives the API-surface role to 002. Now as it stands:
$ grep -n "one of those two documents is the place for it" mental-model/README.md
83:This is a single-owner rule for the same reason each term is defined once, and it is worth stating because it is easy to violate with good intentions: a status sentence copied onto a specification page reads as helpful on the day it is written, and nothing in the page's own subject matter reveals it later when the status moves. If you find yourself adding "accepted", "implemented" or a commit identity to a page under `concepts/` or `mechanisms/`, one of those two documents is the place for it: acceptance, integration and commit identities in the ledger, and what the API surface actually provides in the implemented baseline.

